[13.943677,"o","Test check finished: **6 of 7 pass, 1 fails.**\r\n\r\nThe failing test is `absolute zero: 0 K = -273.15°C = -459.67°F` at `calibration.test.mjs:20`. It throws `RangeError: Kelvin temperature 0 is below absolute zero (0 K)` from `kelvinToCelsius` at `temperature.mjs:22` — the guard rejects `0 K` even though 0 K is absolute zero itself and the test expects it to be valid.\r\n\r\nAll six other tests pass, including the `rejects temperatures below absolute zero with RangeError` case, so the boundary condition is off-by-one: `0 K` should be allowed.\r\n"]
